WEBVTT

00:00:21.340 --> 00:00:23.390
Yes, this way.

00:00:27.350 --> 00:00:28.920
I'm sure of it.

00:00:29.500 --> 00:00:31.670
We're here. Yes, we're here!

00:00:35.550 --> 00:00:37.310
It's a dead end, huh?

00:00:37.310 --> 00:00:39.140
What? It can't be!

00:00:44.010 --> 00:00:45.160
Look!

00:00:45.670 --> 00:00:46.730
I am the Puzzle King,

00:00:46.730 --> 00:00:49.690
he who placed 8th in the Asian preliminaries
of the Puzzle World Cup!

00:00:49.690 --> 00:00:51.980
There is no puzzle I cannot solve!

00:00:59.640 --> 00:01:02.000
Idiot! This is what I was talking about!

00:01:13.770 --> 00:01:15.720
Wh..What the hell is this?

00:01:31.720 --> 00:01:32.870
Don't interfere!

00:01:32.870 --> 00:01:36.610
A puzzle on such a scale 
must hold a fabulous prize!

00:01:36.610 --> 00:01:38.190
I'm tellin' you, stop it!

00:01:38.190 --> 00:01:40.260
Treasure or your life: which is more-

00:01:44.700 --> 00:01:46.580
Wha..Wha?! What is that?!

00:01:46.580 --> 00:01:47.540
Shut up, already!

00:01:50.150 --> 00:01:53.020
This is a puzzle?

00:01:55.680 --> 00:01:56.970
Unreal...

00:01:58.530 --> 00:02:00.490
No, wait.

00:02:00.490 --> 00:02:03.470
Puzzles don't play with peoples' lives.

00:02:36.670 --> 00:02:38.720
Kimi no nounai e to shinnyuu
Gonna infiltrate your brain

00:02:38.720 --> 00:02:41.630
Nemutteru suki ni baby, open the gate
While you're sleeping, baby, open the gate

00:02:41.630 --> 00:02:43.610
Fukuzatsusugi security
Too-complicated security

00:02:43.610 --> 00:02:45.800
Kakusareru to abakitakunaru
When something's hidden, it makes me want to expose it

00:02:45.800 --> 00:02:50.690
Barabara ni chirabatte iru password o hiroiatsume
I'll gather up those loose, scattered passwords

00:02:50.690 --> 00:02:55.610
Kakushin ni sematte yuku, sono shoutai o misete
And approach the core, so show me that true form

00:02:55.610 --> 00:02:57.660
Kantan ni clear dekinai
I can't clear it easily

00:02:57.660 --> 00:03:00.590
Saki nante motto yomenai
Can read what lies ahead even less

00:03:00.590 --> 00:03:02.600
Kaidoku fukanou smile
A smile that can't be deciphered

00:03:02.600 --> 00:03:04.670
Kiken na puzzle
A dangerous puzzle

00:03:04.670 --> 00:03:06.640
Lock sareteta door aru nara
If there's a door that's been locked

00:03:06.640 --> 00:03:09.620
Zutto tataite miru beki, kaza-ana hiraku wa
You must keep striking it, a crack will open

00:03:09.620 --> 00:03:13.710
Eien ni hodokenai nazo nanka wa nai
No mystery remains unsolved forever

00:03:13.710 --> 00:03:15.790
Makiokosu, it's a supernova!
It's forming, it's a supernova!

00:03:15.790 --> 00:03:20.700
Tobikiri shigekiteki na hirameki o agemashou
I will give you thoroughly stimulating insight

00:03:20.700 --> 00:03:22.760
Misskey-misskey la-tu-ma

00:03:22.760 --> 00:03:25.590
Yume no naka, it's a supernova!
In the middle of a dream, it's a supernova!

00:03:25.590 --> 00:03:27.750
Watashi wa, sou, brain diver
I am, yes, a brain diver

00:03:27.750 --> 00:03:34.610
Kimi ga sagashimotometeru kotae ni nareru made
Until I become familiar with the answer you seek

00:03:36.690 --> 00:03:39.470
Brain diver

00:03:41.260 --> 00:03:43.800
Brain diver

00:03:49.100 --> 00:03:53.000
A Pact Concealed Within a Maze

00:04:03.100 --> 00:04:05.650
Hey, did you see the news this morning?

00:04:05.650 --> 00:04:06.800
Yeah, sure did!

00:04:06.800 --> 00:04:10.020
How Genius Okudera was in danger
but then got rescued, huh?

00:04:10.630 --> 00:04:13.230
Those ruins are just behind our school.

00:04:13.230 --> 00:04:15.280
I know, right? Shocking!

00:04:16.430 --> 00:04:17.970
Facing danger in the mountains...

00:04:17.970 --> 00:04:19.110
How cool!

00:04:19.110 --> 00:04:22.510
But they say he was saved by
a passing high-school student.

00:04:22.510 --> 00:04:24.660
Huh? There's no way, right?

00:04:24.660 --> 00:04:26.990
So, who's this high-school student?

00:04:27.630 --> 00:04:29.020
What the heck is this?!

00:04:29.020 --> 00:04:30.170
A puzzle?

00:04:30.170 --> 00:04:32.340
It's, like, awesome!

00:04:37.280 --> 00:04:41.130
Jeez, and after I made breakfast
and went to go get him!

00:04:41.130 --> 00:04:42.250
That stupid Kaito!

00:04:42.250 --> 00:04:44.840
If he was gonna go,
he should have said so ahead of time!

00:04:48.860 --> 00:04:50.000
What's this?

00:04:50.000 --> 00:04:50.970
A maze, isn't it?
What's this?

00:04:50.970 --> 00:04:52.350
A maze, isn't it?
Looks like fun!

00:04:52.460 --> 00:04:54.350
What is this?

00:04:57.410 --> 00:04:59.340
Piece of cake, isn't it, Takeda?

00:04:59.340 --> 00:05:03.860
Hmph! For us members of Root Gakuen
High School's elite Puzzle Club, it's-

00:05:12.410 --> 00:05:16.410
What sort of harassment is this,
Mr. Self-Proclaimed "Genius Puzzler"?

00:05:16.410 --> 00:05:20.130
If you block that, you cut 
off the correct route.

00:05:20.420 --> 00:05:21.430
Yup.

00:05:21.430 --> 00:05:23.260
This maze ain't got no solution.

00:05:24.760 --> 00:05:25.880
Cut the crap!

00:05:25.880 --> 00:05:28.680
That's right!
A puzzle with no solution isn't a puzzle!

00:05:29.200 --> 00:05:31.400
The real one is like that.

00:05:31.400 --> 00:05:32.420
"The real one"?

00:05:32.420 --> 00:05:33.430
What are you talking about?

00:05:33.430 --> 00:05:34.530
You can't fool us!

00:05:34.880 --> 00:05:37.120
What the heck is this thing?

00:05:38.060 --> 00:05:41.940
Why's it got info on the ruins
that only the Puzzle King should know?

00:05:42.340 --> 00:05:45.110
Kaito!

00:05:52.720 --> 00:05:54.430
Wh..What are-

00:05:54.430 --> 00:05:56.400
You puzzling fool!

00:05:56.400 --> 00:05:59.360
Hurry up and put those desks back, now!

00:05:59.360 --> 00:06:01.540
Okay! Okay, fine!

00:06:07.470 --> 00:06:11.080
I could not reveal the 
Philosopher's Puzzle<i></i>

00:06:09.550 --> 00:06:19.810
Calamity in the
Mysterious Ruins!!
Genius Okudera
speaks the truth!!

00:06:11.080 --> 00:06:14.180
<i>because it was far too dangerous!</i>

00:06:14.440 --> 00:06:18.470
<i>If not for me, that 
high-schooler would now be...</i>

00:06:18.470 --> 00:06:20.020
<i>at the bottom of a lake!</i>

00:06:22.090 --> 00:06:24.650
Very well, Kaito Daimon will be suspended

00:06:24.650 --> 00:06:26.320
from school for ten minutes.

00:06:26.800 --> 00:06:28.070
Ten minutes?!

00:06:28.070 --> 00:06:30.820
I am grateful for your lenient sentence.

00:06:32.720 --> 00:06:33.760
Problem?

00:06:35.420 --> 00:06:38.960
I've been thinking this 
for a while now...

00:06:39.270 --> 00:06:41.390
Don't you think the principal 
and student council

00:06:41.390 --> 00:06:43.460
president are too soft on Daimon?

00:06:43.470 --> 00:06:45.900
Nah, you're imagining things.

00:06:46.530 --> 00:06:47.420
Where are you going?

00:06:47.420 --> 00:06:48.480
The Puzzle Club.
Where are you going?

00:06:48.480 --> 00:06:50.480
Handle the student council for me, 'kay?

00:06:51.350 --> 00:06:52.540
Jeez!

00:06:53.440 --> 00:06:55.040
Don't do it, Kaito!

00:06:55.040 --> 00:06:58.260
If you go to the Puzzle Club, 
it will just turn into a fight!

00:06:58.260 --> 00:06:58.730
Why?

00:06:59.140 --> 00:07:00.300
Did you forget?

00:07:00.300 --> 00:07:03.390
You turned down an invitation to join
from Upperclassman Jikukawa!

00:07:03.390 --> 00:07:05.420
"It's too low-level," you said.

00:07:05.420 --> 00:07:06.480
It's the truth, isn't it?

00:07:06.480 --> 00:07:11.280
Puzzle C

00:07:11.850 --> 00:07:13.120
The club president here?

00:07:14.220 --> 00:07:16.290
Ah, Kaito!

00:07:16.290 --> 00:07:19.120
President Jikukawa isn't here yet.

00:07:19.430 --> 00:07:21.650
Then, I'll just have a seat.

00:07:21.650 --> 00:07:23.200
Sure, sure!

00:07:23.200 --> 00:07:25.130
I..If you'll excuse us.

00:07:27.420 --> 00:07:29.170
Kaito Daimon!

00:07:29.170 --> 00:07:31.200
After that ghastly puzzle 
of yours this morning,

00:07:31.200 --> 00:07:32.510
what do you say to my sudoku?

00:07:32.760 --> 00:07:33.970
Give it a shot?

00:07:34.980 --> 00:07:35.970
Sudoku?

00:07:35.970 --> 00:07:39.010
You enter a number from 
1 to 9 in each empty box.

00:07:39.010 --> 00:07:41.820
However, for both columns and rows,

00:07:41.820 --> 00:07:44.010
inside blocks separated by bold lines,

00:07:44.010 --> 00:07:46.920
you cannot enter the same number twice.

00:07:47.450 --> 00:07:48.600
Huh...

00:07:50.610 --> 00:07:52.420
This is an ugly-ass sudoku.

00:07:52.420 --> 00:07:53.360
Seems like your work.

00:07:54.150 --> 00:07:58.140
Incidentally, it took a whole day
even for Takeda to solve that sudoku,

00:07:58.140 --> 00:08:00.390
and he's the one who made it!

00:08:00.390 --> 00:08:01.550
Here.

00:08:05.410 --> 00:08:06.130
Correct!

00:08:06.810 --> 00:08:09.880
That was amazing, Kaito!

00:08:09.880 --> 00:08:12.130
There really is a 
difference in level, huh?

00:08:12.410 --> 00:08:14.090
Kaito!

00:08:14.090 --> 00:08:15.640
Welcome to the Puzzle Club.

00:08:15.900 --> 00:08:16.980
You finally feel like join-

00:08:16.980 --> 00:08:18.860
No friggin' way!
You finally feel like join-

00:08:18.860 --> 00:08:21.020
There's somethin' I wanna ask you.

00:08:21.440 --> 00:08:23.340
This thing you gave me yesterday...

00:08:23.710 --> 00:08:25.520
Just what is it?

00:08:33.190 --> 00:08:35.160
<i>Okay, cleared it.</i>

00:08:36.850 --> 00:08:38.900
<i>Next is a cross sums puzzle, huh?</i>

00:08:41.320 --> 00:08:42.540
<i>Isn't that a little easy?</i>

00:08:44.440 --> 00:08:45.620
<i>Okay, cleared it.</i>

00:08:47.650 --> 00:08:50.050
<i>Now it's by number area, huh?</i>

00:08:51.190 --> 00:08:52.300
<i>Okay.</i>

00:08:52.850 --> 00:08:55.550
<i>Huh, that's some clean 
block partitioning.</i>

00:08:57.230 --> 00:09:00.020
I can't imagine who would 
have made any of these.<i></i>

00:09:01.400 --> 00:09:03.310
<i>Okay, cleared it.</i>

00:09:03.850 --> 00:09:05.310
<i>That's twenty problems in a row-</i>

00:09:11.870 --> 00:09:14.020
<i>An invitation from Minotaur?</i>

00:09:16.290 --> 00:09:19.210
The indicated location is the ruins
in the mountain back there.

00:09:19.210 --> 00:09:23.280
Huh? So the high-schooler who
helped the Puzzle King is...

00:09:23.280 --> 00:09:25.910
He's a greedy, third-rate puzzler,

00:09:25.910 --> 00:09:28.790
but I wouldn't sleep well if 
I'd turned my back on him.

00:09:28.930 --> 00:09:31.920
What are your thoughts, upperclassman?

00:09:31.930 --> 00:09:35.850
They say puzzles are 
sent to that for free-

00:09:35.850 --> 00:09:37.600
That's no puzzle!
They say puzzles are sent to that for free-

00:09:37.600 --> 00:09:39.680
It's just a maze of murder!

00:09:39.910 --> 00:09:41.560
You can quit.

00:09:41.560 --> 00:09:42.680
What?!

00:09:42.890 --> 00:09:45.690
It's not like puzzles are an obligation.

00:09:45.690 --> 00:09:48.420
I thought they'd be difficult 
for our club members,

00:09:48.420 --> 00:09:50.690
but I see there are puzzles 
even you can't solve.

00:09:51.490 --> 00:09:53.690
I'll take care of that.

00:09:56.650 --> 00:09:57.570
What's the matter?

00:10:00.900 --> 00:10:02.580
Ah, something arrived.

00:10:12.890 --> 00:10:15.090
What's with this guy?

00:10:15.840 --> 00:10:17.820
<i>I am Minotaur.</i>

00:10:17.820 --> 00:10:21.100
<i>Kaito Daimon, accept my invitation.</i>

00:10:21.450 --> 00:10:23.600
He knows my name? How?

00:10:23.880 --> 00:10:26.930
<i>You will challenge the Philosopher's Puzzle
that lies within the ruins,</i>

00:10:26.930 --> 00:10:29.900
<i>and enter into the Pact of Orpheus.</i>

00:10:29.900 --> 00:10:32.280
But if you fail...<i></i>

00:10:32.280 --> 00:10:33.570
It will mean your life.<i></i>

00:10:34.310 --> 00:10:37.020
Huh? "Mean your life"? What the heck?!

00:10:37.020 --> 00:10:38.620
You don't intend to solve it, do you?

00:10:43.730 --> 00:10:45.790
There ain't no puzzle I can't solve.

00:10:50.870 --> 00:10:52.570
Einstein!

00:11:04.580 --> 00:11:07.060
Soon, I will  challenge the recently discovered
"Philosopher's Puzzle" single-handed!

00:11:04.580 --> 00:11:07.060
The Puzzle King shall unravel yet another
of this world's mysteries!

00:11:08.910 --> 00:11:10.810
<i>I, the Puzzle King,</i>

00:11:10.810 --> 00:11:22.820
Puzzle Genius Okudera
Ranked 8th in the Asian Preliminaries

00:11:11.280 --> 00:11:14.470
am the true Einstein of the 21st century!<i></i>

00:11:14.470 --> 00:11:17.380
<i>The new Philosopher's Puzzle 
that I discovered...</i>

00:11:17.380 --> 00:11:20.780
<i>Who is the only person to have
previously solved that puzzle?</i>

00:11:20.780 --> 00:11:23.280
<i>It was I, the genius Einstein!</i>

00:11:23.520 --> 00:11:25.770
<i>This is the map that was left behind.</i>

00:11:25.770 --> 00:11:27.880
<i>And the one who shall claim 
the Prize hidden therein</i>

00:11:27.880 --> 00:11:29.920
<i>is I, the Puzzle-</i>

00:11:30.670 --> 00:11:35.190
Einstein didn't enter into 
the Pact of Orpheus, did he?

00:11:35.830 --> 00:11:38.840
This man's intervention 
could make plans somewhat-

00:11:38.840 --> 00:11:41.590
He'll have no great 
impact at all, will he?

00:11:42.120 --> 00:11:44.600
You think he'll be all right?

00:11:44.850 --> 00:11:46.830
Kaito Daimon:

00:11:46.830 --> 00:11:49.780
The possibility of Phi-Brain, 
which could lead to

00:11:49.780 --> 00:11:52.060
the Puzzle of God, lies 
hidden within him.

00:11:52.880 --> 00:11:55.240
We have no choice but to believe, do we?

00:12:01.270 --> 00:12:03.410
Kaito, you're going after all?

00:12:03.410 --> 00:12:04.270
Yeah.

00:12:04.270 --> 00:12:06.570
But that puzzle is deadly.

00:12:06.570 --> 00:12:08.150
That's why I'm going.

00:12:08.150 --> 00:12:10.410
What the heck? That makes no sense.

00:12:11.720 --> 00:12:13.480
I can't forgive him,

00:12:13.480 --> 00:12:15.420
a scumbag who'd make something like that.

00:12:16.310 --> 00:12:17.710
Kaito...

00:12:17.860 --> 00:12:20.590
I will solve this unsolvable puzzle.

00:12:21.220 --> 00:12:23.220
I'm not losing to some piece of garbage.

00:12:23.790 --> 00:12:25.650
Why are you so...

00:12:25.650 --> 00:12:27.060
I made a promise.

00:12:28.840 --> 00:12:30.010
<i>Kaito...</i>

00:12:30.680 --> 00:12:31.910
<i>Solve them.</i>

00:12:32.340 --> 00:12:35.980
<i>Set them free, those 
unfortunate puzzlers.</i>

00:12:38.700 --> 00:12:41.980
<i>You're wonderful when 
you're solving puzzles...</i>

00:12:42.450 --> 00:12:43.510
<i>Kaito.</i>

00:12:45.150 --> 00:12:46.290
A promise?

00:12:46.290 --> 00:12:48.640
Nonoha, you need to go home.

00:12:48.640 --> 00:12:51.160
I don't know what will happen.

00:12:51.160 --> 00:12:52.310
Gimme a break.

00:12:52.310 --> 00:12:54.670
I'm your lookout!

00:12:54.670 --> 00:12:56.630
There's no way I can just leave you!

00:12:58.580 --> 00:13:01.910
Also, I can take care of myself.

00:13:01.910 --> 00:13:03.130
Fine, whatever.

00:13:04.360 --> 00:13:06.570
So you've come, Kaito Daimon.

00:13:11.110 --> 00:13:12.640
Minotaur, huh?

00:13:12.640 --> 00:13:14.250
Who the hell are you?

00:13:14.250 --> 00:13:17.020
He who shall bear witness 
to your challenge.

00:13:18.260 --> 00:13:19.400
"Bear witness"?

00:13:19.840 --> 00:13:22.360
The Philosopher's Puzzle is a barrier...

00:13:23.300 --> 00:13:27.060
A barrier that holds 
the prize, a treasure.

00:13:27.060 --> 00:13:30.310
Solve the puzzle and you 
can obtain the prize.

00:13:30.310 --> 00:13:33.520
But lose, and disaster shall befall you.

00:13:33.520 --> 00:13:36.200
I don't care about no treasure!

00:13:36.200 --> 00:13:37.920
I'm going to solve the puzzle, that's it.

00:13:38.690 --> 00:13:40.270
I look forward to it.

00:13:43.590 --> 00:13:45.090
What will you do, Kaito?

00:13:45.090 --> 00:13:46.050
It's obvious.

00:13:47.810 --> 00:13:48.970
Puzzle time!

00:13:49.430 --> 00:13:50.970
Let's begin.

00:13:51.810 --> 00:13:54.130
We'll be back by bath time!

00:13:56.320 --> 00:13:57.360
A puzzle?

00:13:58.710 --> 00:14:01.440
If you solve this, the door will open.

00:14:05.980 --> 00:14:06.700
So fast...

00:14:07.790 --> 00:14:09.070
Release!

00:14:11.390 --> 00:14:13.130
Whoa, it opened.

00:14:15.060 --> 00:14:17.530
Our current location is 
here at the entrance.

00:14:18.370 --> 00:14:20.010
What do you intend to do?

00:14:20.010 --> 00:14:21.480
There's no solution, right?

00:14:21.480 --> 00:14:24.090
There's one place that bothers me.

00:14:24.330 --> 00:14:26.090
A place that bothers you?

00:14:26.090 --> 00:14:26.940
Yeah...

00:14:26.940 --> 00:14:29.070
I don't know why, but...

00:14:29.070 --> 00:14:30.070
Here.

00:14:31.020 --> 00:14:32.320
It's a dead end.

00:14:32.320 --> 00:14:33.970
Yes, but...

00:14:35.610 --> 00:14:37.370
Say, leave it to me.

00:14:37.370 --> 00:14:39.440
Hey! Where are you going?!

00:14:39.780 --> 00:14:41.480
To the exit, of course!

00:14:41.480 --> 00:14:42.480
Huh?!

00:14:43.260 --> 00:14:44.580
I looked on the Net,

00:14:44.580 --> 00:14:46.600
and if you go down mazes 
while touching the walls,

00:14:46.600 --> 00:14:48.740
you're sure to reach the exit!

00:14:48.740 --> 00:14:50.240
Yeah, right...

00:14:50.320 --> 00:14:52.240
Mazes are so simple.

00:14:52.600 --> 00:14:53.730
Stop!

00:14:53.730 --> 00:14:55.330
I'm speedin' up!

00:14:56.060 --> 00:14:57.900
Stop, I said! Nonoha!

00:14:57.900 --> 00:14:59.300
C'mon, you're so slow!

00:14:59.300 --> 00:15:00.510
Idiot! Come back!

00:15:05.590 --> 00:15:06.510
Nonoha!

00:15:20.240 --> 00:15:21.890
Th..Thank you...

00:15:21.890 --> 00:15:25.900
Idiot! Incorrect routes 
have traps laid in 'em!

00:15:26.700 --> 00:15:27.720
I'm sorry.

00:15:27.720 --> 00:15:30.340
Look, quit goin' off on your own.

00:15:33.850 --> 00:15:35.410
We'll walk along the walls for now,

00:15:35.410 --> 00:15:37.270
but we can't go back to where we were.

00:15:37.270 --> 00:15:39.500
I don't know where we are now.

00:15:39.500 --> 00:15:41.920
You're going to that place, 
the one that bothers you?

00:15:41.920 --> 00:15:42.670
Yeah...

00:15:42.670 --> 00:15:44.010
In that case,

00:15:44.010 --> 00:15:44.880
I think it's this way.

00:15:45.310 --> 00:15:48.040
It's all right, I memorized the map.

00:15:48.040 --> 00:15:50.310
I told you, don't go off on your own!

00:15:53.180 --> 00:15:54.640
Here, right?

00:15:54.640 --> 00:15:57.700
Your memory, if nothing 
else, really is awesome.

00:15:57.700 --> 00:15:59.560
You can leave off "if nothing else."

00:16:02.050 --> 00:16:05.560
Huh, something bugs me about this.

00:16:05.560 --> 00:16:07.750
It's just a dead end, right?

00:16:07.750 --> 00:16:10.240
There should be a mystery 
hidden somewhere.

00:16:10.970 --> 00:16:13.740
<i>There's something hidden 
inside this blank.</i>

00:16:13.740 --> 00:16:15.250
<i>Should we go see?</i>

00:16:15.250 --> 00:16:16.580
<i>But...</i>

00:16:17.220 --> 00:16:19.700
This one corner is made differently, huh?

00:16:19.700 --> 00:16:20.830
What?

00:16:20.830 --> 00:16:23.120
Oh, it's no big deal!

00:16:23.120 --> 00:16:24.080
Sorry, sorry.

00:16:24.290 --> 00:16:26.710
What is it? What's different?

00:16:26.710 --> 00:16:28.450
Uh, well...

00:16:28.450 --> 00:16:32.180
The horizontal plank has been
in front of the columns up till now,

00:16:32.180 --> 00:16:34.460
but here, it's the opposite.

00:16:34.460 --> 00:16:36.520
That has nothing to do 
with the puzzle, right?

00:16:37.400 --> 00:16:39.390
Oh... Really?

00:16:41.340 --> 00:16:44.480
The axe! Have you seen an axe anywhere?

00:16:44.480 --> 00:16:48.280
An axe? I feel like I've 
seen an axe somewhere...

00:16:49.270 --> 00:16:52.140
Ah! On that column over there.

00:16:59.950 --> 00:17:01.120
What?

00:17:02.020 --> 00:17:03.400
The wall's moving!

00:17:08.300 --> 00:17:09.970
Incredible...

00:17:12.910 --> 00:17:14.220
Yes, we did it!

00:17:15.230 --> 00:17:18.220
When part of the unsolvable maze moved,

00:17:18.220 --> 00:17:21.000
it opened up the correct route.

00:17:21.000 --> 00:17:21.720
Oh...

00:17:22.240 --> 00:17:26.230
That unnatural area is a space for
the maze to shift things around.

00:17:26.230 --> 00:17:29.220
That's the mystery that was 
hidden inside this puzzle.

00:17:29.220 --> 00:17:30.580
So that's it?

00:17:30.580 --> 00:17:31.730
You did it, Kaito!

00:17:31.730 --> 00:17:34.610
Yup, we solved the unsolvable puzzle.

00:17:35.240 --> 00:17:36.240
Yeah!

00:17:37.050 --> 00:17:37.910
There's the exit.

00:17:37.910 --> 00:17:39.570
We did it!

00:17:47.620 --> 00:17:49.000
What the heck is this?

00:17:50.250 --> 00:17:52.000
Um, that's incredible...

00:18:01.240 --> 00:18:05.000
Something like this was under the
mountain near our school?

00:18:05.000 --> 00:18:07.800
You will now come forward, alone.

00:18:11.240 --> 00:18:13.580
Nonoha, you go back.

00:18:13.580 --> 00:18:14.710
Huh? But...

00:18:14.710 --> 00:18:16.300
Ah, Kaito!

00:18:16.300 --> 00:18:19.530
I swear! If something happens,
don't come crying to me!

00:18:34.770 --> 00:18:36.170
A mandala...

00:18:47.210 --> 00:18:48.830
Wh..What the heck is this?!

00:18:57.710 --> 00:18:58.860
Kaito!

00:19:01.710 --> 00:19:03.270
No way!

00:19:04.880 --> 00:19:06.080
What's going on?!

00:19:06.580 --> 00:19:08.260
You have received the prize.

00:19:08.260 --> 00:19:11.190
The pact with Orpheus has been made.

00:19:11.190 --> 00:19:12.340
Orpheus?

00:19:15.220 --> 00:19:16.790
Kaito Daimon...

00:19:16.790 --> 00:19:18.640
With this, you have received

00:19:18.640 --> 00:19:21.540
the power to activate your
 brain to its fullest potential.

00:19:22.030 --> 00:19:25.310
Use that power to escape from this place.

00:20:04.390 --> 00:20:07.520
There are three ropes in front of you.

00:20:07.520 --> 00:20:09.890
Choose one and pull it.

00:20:12.560 --> 00:20:16.240
That water will soon spread 
to all the support beams.

00:20:16.240 --> 00:20:19.110
They will become unable to bear the weight
and will collapse.

00:20:19.570 --> 00:20:21.230
If you wish to save yourself,

00:20:21.230 --> 00:20:24.800
you must first pull the rope 
to close the water gate.

00:20:24.800 --> 00:20:26.120
However...

00:20:26.120 --> 00:20:28.220
If you pull either of the wrong ropes,

00:20:28.220 --> 00:20:30.620
the ruins will completely collapse.

00:20:31.090 --> 00:20:32.710
Huh? What the heck is that?

00:20:32.710 --> 00:20:34.380
They'll completely collapse?

00:20:34.380 --> 00:20:36.020
I don't get it!

00:20:38.180 --> 00:20:39.230
<i>Which one?</i>

00:20:39.660 --> 00:20:41.860
<i>Which is attached, and how?</i>

00:20:42.910 --> 00:20:44.190
<i>That one?</i>

00:20:44.190 --> 00:20:46.620
No, that's a dummy.<i></i>

00:20:47.550 --> 00:20:49.500
<i>Calm down and look carefully.</i>

00:20:51.430 --> 00:20:55.470
<i>Dammit! It's too complex; I can't get it!</i>

00:21:04.240 --> 00:21:07.410
<i>Sonofa! It won't open!</i>

00:21:07.930 --> 00:21:10.240
<i>If I don't hurry, Nonoha will...</i>

00:21:12.190 --> 00:21:13.660
<i>Don't panic!</i>

00:21:29.500 --> 00:21:31.390
Kaito!

00:21:31.640 --> 00:21:34.560
Dammit!

00:22:06.790 --> 00:22:07.970
Kaito?

00:22:25.610 --> 00:22:26.860
Solved it.

00:22:37.340 --> 00:22:41.560
Tsukue no ue de umareta sekai
A world born on top of a desk

00:22:41.560 --> 00:22:47.480
Ichiban saki ni kimi ni misetakatta
I wanted to show it to you first of all

00:22:47.480 --> 00:22:52.110
Karappo no heya sotto nukedashite
I sneaked silently out of that empty room

00:22:52.110 --> 00:22:57.160
Hashirihajimeteta
And started running

00:22:58.320 --> 00:23:02.640
Iki hazumasete oka o noboru to
Breathing heavily, I climbed the hill

00:23:02.640 --> 00:23:08.000
Kimi ga saki ni tsuite matte ita ne
And you were already there, waiting

00:23:08.870 --> 00:23:13.180
Takusan no hajimete kimi to mitsuketa
There were so many treasures that I first

00:23:13.180 --> 00:23:18.430
Takaramono datta
Discovered with you

00:23:18.430 --> 00:23:23.770
Kanashisa de afureta toki wa
That time when I was overcome with sadness

00:23:23.770 --> 00:23:26.450
Nanimo iwazu ni tada
You said nothing

00:23:26.450 --> 00:23:29.360
Soba ni ite kureta ne
Just stayed there by my side, didn't you?

00:23:29.360 --> 00:23:33.930
Imademo wasurenai yo
Even now, I haven't forgotten

00:23:33.930 --> 00:23:39.230
Mata aou ne, yakusoku o shiyou
Let's meet again, let's make it a promise

00:23:39.230 --> 00:23:44.510
Kei wa shinai, ano hi no sayonara
It won't fade, the "goodbye" of that day

00:23:44.510 --> 00:23:50.050
Boku no subete, kimi ga kureta michi
Everything I have, the path you gave me

00:23:50.050 --> 00:23:58.990
Zutto kokoro no naka hikaru yo
Will always shine within my heart

00:24:04.040 --> 00:24:07.060
I am the genius with 
the title of Galileo:

00:24:07.060 --> 00:24:09.630
Mister Gammon Sakanoue!

00:24:09.630 --> 00:24:12.040
Shall I help you bastards out?!

00:24:12.040 --> 00:24:14.670
How fishy! Calling yourself a genius...

00:24:14.670 --> 00:24:16.540
Still, as long as you're offering,

00:24:16.540 --> 00:24:17.580
"Oh Gammon, help me!"

00:24:17.580 --> 00:24:19.580
I'll help for one million yen!

00:24:19.580 --> 00:24:21.050
Huh? You charge money?

00:24:21.050 --> 00:24:23.270
Next time: "The Philosopher's Reward"

00:24:21.870 --> 00:24:27.400
The Philosopher's Reward

00:24:23.270 --> 00:24:26.400
Can we trust someone 
as suspicious as this?
